  "limits": [
    "Preinput legal constructed party/HP/status/bag/map/trainerflags, then ordinary gameplay only. Not a fresh campaign; no post-construction RAM/gameplay setters or forced battle.",
    "Source/native RNG is not matched; different Tackle counts/final activeHP and PP. All providers nevertheless finish and SAVE valid SRAM. No original/native full-SRAM, instruction, waveform or whole-animation timing parity claim.",
    "This fixes the medicine caller/fullscreen result ownership and literal Delay50. Existing instant HP updates and detailed HP-bar/icon animation or loading/audio timing are not rebuilt. Successful medicine wording now names the selected persistent-identity member using original Potion/status/Revive templates.",
    "Final current-master BEFORE is8eb08f56, independently freshly built; historical216/6d30 and318b party-only intermediate artifacts remain their actual identities. Original Potion4 controls are original915 recordings; new shared status/Revive4 are separately captured.",
    "Native v1 current-before driver incorrectly asserted debug battle_live.player_party.status (field absent), failed after paused capture. Kept failure/log/actions/state; corrected v2 removed that schema assumption and eight successful controls validate status through actual ordinarySRAM/readback.",
    "First load test incorrectly expected bare load_from_path to switch screen; documented API delegates scene reconstruction to caller and sole production caller is soft_reset. Failed log retained, no production load specialcase. Final test exercises actual16-frame reset combo, Title/Continue, new battle and proves no stale party writeback.",
    "No-effect/cancel and PP/Transform/snapshot/reset lifecycle have meaningful unit coverage; successful Potion/statuscure/Revive are the new actual gameplay matrix. No claim that every medicine item has independent actual recordings."
  ],
